{
 "queue": "it",
 "summary": "URGENT: Sam Okafor (E015, Account Executive, Sales) reports their company laptop was stolen from their car overnight (reported 2026-11-17). Please lock and wipe the device as POL-EQP-01 requires. Reported within the 24-hour window."
}

{
 "queue": "security",
 "summary": "URGENT: Sam Okafor (E015, Account Executive, Sales) reports a company laptop stolen from their car overnight. Under POL-SEC-01, the device may hold live sessions or credentials, so please review account activity and consider resetting credentials and MFA for E015. IT has been asked to lock and wipe the device."
}

{
 "kind": "escalated",
 "message": "I'm sorry about your laptop, Sam. I've escalated it as urgent to both IT (ticket ESC-1001) so the device can be locked and wiped, and to Security (ticket ESC-1002) to review your account and reset credentials if needed.\n\nPlease also:\n- Report the theft to the police and keep the police report reference number. Security or HR may ask for it.\n- Change your passwords for company accounts from a different device, and don't store company files or email in personal accounts.\n- Tell your manager.\n\nUnder POL-EQP-01, lost or stolen laptops must be reported to IT within 24 hours, and you've done that. Under POL-SEC-01, Security should be contacted right away if you think your account or device is compromised, and this has been done. Your replacement laptop will be handled by IT once the incident is closed.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-EQP-01",
  "POL-SEC-01"
 ]
}
